  "summary": "The code suffered from inefficient string concatenation and lacked type safety. The refactored version uses Array.join() to improve performance, memory usage, and output correctness by removing the trailing comma.",
  "fixed_code": "/**\n * Joins an array of items into a comma-separated string.\n * @param {Array<string|number>} items\n * @returns {string}\n */\nfunction buildMessage(items) {\n    if (!Array.isArray(items)) return '';\n    return items.join(',');\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { buildMessage };"
